-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rapp</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Shumaker</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Conjugated equine estrogens and global cognitive function in postmenopausal women</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>291</volume><fpage>2959</fpage><lpage>68</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15213207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Funkenstein</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Albert</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Prevalence of Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease in a community population of older persons: higher than previously reported</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>262</volume><fpage>2551</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2810583</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>FDA</collab><year>2003</year><article-title>FDA approves lower dose of Prempro, a combination estrogen and progestin drug for postmenopausal women</article-title><source>FDA News</source><month>3</month><day>13</day></citation></ref><ref id="b23-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flicker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferris</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Reisberg</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Mild cognitive impairment in the elderly: predictors of dementia</article-title><source>Neurology</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>1006</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2067629</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b24-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Folstein</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Folstein</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>McHugh</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1975</year><article-title>&#x0201c;Mini-mental state&#x0201d;: a practical method for grading the cognitive state of patients for the clinician&#x0201d;</article-title><source>J Psychiatr Res</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1202204</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fouad</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Corbie-Smith</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Curb</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Special populations recruitment for the Women&#x02019;s Health Initiative: successes and limitations</article-title><source>Control Clin Trials</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>335</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15296809</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friedland</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Farrer</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cupples</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Smoking and risk of Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>352</volume><fpage>819</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9737315</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gapstur</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Potter</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Sellers</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Increased risk of breast cancer with alcohol consumption in postmenopausal women</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><volume>136</volume><fpage>1221</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1476144</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b28-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garcia-Segura</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><conf-name>Plenary Conference at the 8th Meeting of the Portuguese Society of Neurosciences</conf-name></citation></ref><ref id="b29-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Geerlings</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Launer</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>de Jong</surname><given-names>FH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><collab>Rotterdam Study</collab><year>2003</year><article-title>Endogenous estradiol and risk of dementia in women and men: the Rotterdam Study</article-title><source>Ann Neurol</source><volume>53</volume><fpage>607</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12730994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b30-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gelfand</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Testosterone-mediated neuroprotection through the androgen receptor in human primary neurons</article-title><source>J Neurochem</source><volume>77</volume><fpage>1319</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11389183</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b31-ndt-2-199"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibbs</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Burke</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></